cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Whybook in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Whybook: a question-driven view of Jupyter notebooks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Krassowski
    given-names: Michał
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/openteams-ai/whybook"
url: "https://whybook.dev"
abstract: >-
  Whybook is a JupyterLab extension: a view of a Jupyter notebook for asking
  questions about data and understanding every result. The analyst picks one of
  the questions it offers, or asks their own; the answer becomes an ordinary
  notebook cell, and every constant, default and choice behind the result shows
  on the cell.
keywords:
  - jupyter
  - jupyterlab
  - exploratory data analysis
  - statistics
  - human-in-the-loop
